{"id": "EUVD-2021-34876", "enisaUuid": "b7cdb45f-6df8-3180-8bed-4660b0c84a9e", "description": "PocketMine-MP before 4.0.3 does not perform case-insensitive matching when removing operator entries from ops.txt. The removeOp function lowercases the supplied name but only removes an exactly matching entry, so an operator name stored with non-lowercase letters cannot be revoked using the deop command, leaving the player as an operator until the entry is removed from ops.txt manually.", "datePublished": "2026-09-06T12:00:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:20:52", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pmmp/PocketMine-MP/security/advisories/GHSA-j5qg-w9jg-3wg3", "https://github.com/pmmp/PocketMine-MP/commit/4d37b79ff7f9d9452e988387f97919a9a1c4954e", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/pocketmine-mp-before-4.0.3-operator-privilege-escalation-via-case-sensitivity"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5mrr-24gh-4jwh", "CVE-2021-48006"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "903f945f-c5d3-3ca8-a384-4dcc644be95d", "product": {"name": "PocketMine-MP", "vendor": {"name": "pmmp"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.0.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "67169e70-f8c5-39c7-81fc-23e853260f59", "vendor": {"name": "pmmp"}}], "isExploited": false}